From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: ieframe: an internet shortcut saves while its caller holds the property set open

WiX's internet shortcut custom action (every WiX-built MSI with a website
link in the Start menu: Node.js's) opens the shortcut's property set for
writing, then IPersistFile::Save while it is still open. Save wrote the
file, then failed with STG_E_ACCESSDENIED opening the property set to read
the icon, and the install rolled back (MSI error 1603). The file is written
all the same and Save succeeds.

Gate: test/appfix-gate.sh.
---
--- a/dlls/ieframe/intshcut.c
+++ b/dlls/ieframe/intshcut.c
@@ -630,7 +630,11 @@
             }
             else
             {
-               TRACE("Unable to get the IPropertyStorage.\n");
+               /* The caller may hold the property set open itself (WiX's
+                * internet shortcut action does, to set an icon): the file is
+                * written all the same. */
+               TRACE("Unable to get the IPropertyStorage, hr %#lx.\n", hr);
+               hr = S_OK;
             }
 
             CloseHandle(file);
